messages:
Maya: quick heads-up — PR #3456 merged but I noticed two doc regressions: examples still use `action` instead of `tool`, and the TS SDK snippet shows the old `.callTool(...)` API. Should be a tiny follow-up PR.

Sam: ok thanks for catching. do we have a migration blurb we can drop in the quickstart? I can update the TS snippet but want to avoid breaking links used in marketing.

Lina: the quickstart links to /docs/guides/tool-calling (sidebar pinned). if we change examples, add a short 'v2 field names' note at the top of that page mapping action -> tool. low friction.

Omar: +1. also the structured-output page doesn't show our recommended parse-fallback pattern (validate -> try-parse -> fallback). we should add a minimal example for both py/ts.

Maya: proposed fallback pattern (python) — feel free to eyeball and tweak:

Maya: ```python
# validate -> try parse -> fallback
schema = {"type": "object", "properties": {"tool": {"type": "string"}}}
raw = llm_response
if validate(raw, schema):
    result = parse_json(raw)
else:
    result = {"tool": "unknown", "raw_text": raw}
```

Sam: nice. can we add a compact TS version? lots of users ask for TS-first snippets.

Lina: quick TS draft I hacked together:

Lina: ```ts
// soft-parse pattern
const raw = await client.generate(prompt)
try {
  const payload = JSON.parse(raw.text)
  if (payload && payload.tool) return payload
} catch (e) {
  // fall through
}
return { tool: 'unknown', raw: raw.text }
```

Omar: I also found two dead links in the PR — one to an external gist containing a schema and one to an old SDK path. I'll replace the gist with the inline schema example and point the SDK link to /sdk/ts/function-calling.

Maya: UX ask: add a short note like "Note: older examples used 'action' — map action -> tool" so folks running old samples don't get confused.

Sam: will open a small follow-up PR to update quickstart copy, add the migration note, and include the TS snippet. tagging @Lina for review.

Lina: can we also add a docs-ci lint to grep rendered pages for the string "tool" in example blocks? i'll add a quick grep step so future regressions get caught.

docs-bot: Reminder — docs PR template requires a CHANGELOG entry for user-visible example changes. Please add a brief line in docs/CHANGELOG.md.

Maya: Sam — can you add the changelog line to your branch? once that's in i'll squash+merge after Lina approves.

Sam: pushing a commit now with the TS snippet update, migration note, and changelog line. will ping when CI passes.

Omar: after merge i'll smoke-test the quickstart links and close tracking issue (#901). ping if you see any broken anchors post-deploy.

Maya: thanks all — this should clear a few support tickets. :thumbsup:
